        "type": "the-purpose",
        "title": "Untitled",
        "body": "This topic set is designed to provide a comprehensive, yet conceptually accessible, exploration of Black Holes for a self-learner without a formal background in mathematics or advanced science. The topics intentionally avoid complex equations and instead focus on the \"why,\" \"how,\" and \"so what\" of these cosmic objects. They cover the full life cycle of black holes, from their formation to their profound influence on galaxies. The set also explores the ingenious methods astronomers use to observe these \"invisible\" objects and delves into the mind-bending theoretical puzzles, like the Information Paradox, that challenge our understanding of reality. These topics are structured to be intellectually engaging and challenging, fostering a deep conceptual understanding of modern cosmology.",
        "line_number": 27,
        "source": "topic-set-conceptual-guide-to-black-holes-🆔20251106223419.md",
