        },
        {
          "text": "**Accretion Disks vs. Jets:** What is the mechanism that \"feeds\" a black hole (the disk) and what is the mechanism that shoots out energy (the jet)? Why do some have jets and others don't?",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 118,
          "source": "topic-set-conceptual-guide-to-black-holes-🆔20251106223419.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**The \"No-Hair\" Theorem:** The conceptual idea that a black hole, once formed, can be described by only three properties: its **mass**, its **spin** (angular momentum), and its **electric charge**.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 118,
          "source": "topic-set-conceptual-guide-to-black-holes-🆔20251106223419.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Hawking Radiation:** The purely theoretical, conceptual process by which black holes can slowly \"evaporate\" over trillions of years by emitting particles from their event horizon.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 123,
          "source": "topic-set-conceptual-guide-to-black-holes-🆔20251106223419.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Stellar-Mass vs. Intermediate-Mass vs. Supermassive:** Understanding the different \"weight classes\" of black holes and why the \"middle\" (intermediate) ones are so hard to find.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 132,
          "source": "topic-set-conceptual-guide-to-black-holes-🆔20251106223419.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Quasars and Active Galactic Nuclei (AGN):** These are not black holes themselves, but the *phenomenon* of a supermassive black hole that is actively and brightly \"feeding\" at the center of a distant galaxy.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 134,
          "source": "topic-set-conceptual-guide-to-black-holes-🆔20251106223419.md"
        }
      ]
